/**
@defgroup core Core module
@brief Module entry point, shared utilities and project-wide settings.

@defgroup services Services
@brief Game instance subsystems that talk to the backend and convert coordinates.

Every service is a UGameInstanceSubsystem, so Unreal creates one instance per game
instance and keeps it alive across level loads.

@defgroup backend Backend abstraction
@ingroup services
@brief Interfaces that hide the Eclipse Ditto specifics (REST, event stream, envelope
format) from the rest of the viewer, plus their Ditto implementations.

@defgroup entities Entities
@brief The world actor that represents a digital twin thing, the factory that spawns
it and the registry of entity types.

@defgroup entitystructs Entity data structs
@brief USTRUCT schemas that mirror the JSON of each Ditto thing type.

FJsonObjectConverter fills these structs from the thing JSON at runtime, so field names
match the JSON keys exactly, including the Portuguese ones.

@defgroup entitystructs_deprecated Deprecated entity structs
@ingroup entitystructs
@brief Schemas for thing types that the backend no longer publishes. Kept so older
data sets still load.

@defgroup entitydeps Entity type extensions
@brief Per-type behaviour plugged into the generic entity actor: models, badges,
geometry meshes, fire simulation, toll camera animation and similar.

@defgroup gameplay Gameplay
@brief Game modes, player controllers, the camera pawn and its movement components.

@defgroup managers Managers
@brief Local player subsystems for selection and UI state.

@defgroup ui User interface
@brief UMG widgets, the theme system and the JSON viewer.

@defgroup signbenchmark Sign benchmark
@brief Standalone harness that measures different strategies for spawning road sign
models. Not used by the viewer itself.
*/
